<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sunderlal Committee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sunderlal Committee Report</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sunderlal Committee was a goodwill mission sent by the Indian government in late 1948, led by the Congress politician Pandit Sunderlal, to investigate violence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a> after its annexation. Its report estimated that between 27,000 and 40,000 Muslims had been killed during and after the military operation. The report was not published and only became public decades later.</p></div>
